ore_insider_own":2.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Skyworks Solutions, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, develops, manufactures, and markets analog and mixed-signal semiconductor products and solutions in the United States, Taiwan, China, South Korea, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. The company offers amplifiers, antenna tuners, attenuators, automotive tuners and digital radios, wireless ASoC, DC/DC converters, demodulators, detectors, digital power isolators, diodes, directional couplers, diversity receive modules, filters, front-end modules, hybrids, light emitting diode drivers, low noise amplifiers, mixers, modulators, and optocouplers/optoisolators. It also provides phase locked loops, phase shifters, power dividers/combiners, power over ethernet, power isolators, ProSLIC family of subscriber line interface circuits, receivers, system in package, switches, synthesizers, timing devices, voltage-controlled oscillators/synthesizers, and voltage regulators. The company sells its products through direct sales force, electronic component distributors, and independent sales representatives. Its products are used in aerospace, automotive, broadband, cellular infrastructure, connected home, defense, entertainment and gaming, industrial, medical, smartphone, tablet, and wearables applications. The company was founded in 1962 and is headquartered in Irvine, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip Gordon Brace | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Skyworks Solutions, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $19.3B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 11% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.73\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -10.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 99% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.991809311554318},{"text":"Payout ratio of 147% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Zacks Research Upgrades Skyworks Solutions (NASDAQ:SWKS) to \u201cStrong-Buy\u201d","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/zacks-research-upgrades-skyworks-solutions-nasdaqswks-to-strong-buy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973540.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"All You Need to Know About Skyworks (SWKS) Rating Upgrade to Strong Buy","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024632/all-you-need-to-know-about-skyworks-swks-rating-upgrade-to-strong-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3024632","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Karilee Durham Acquires 8,806 Shares Through Performance Award at Skyworks Solutions","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/karilee-durham-acquires-8806-shares-through-performance-award-at-skyworks-solutions","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794009730.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.751,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Skyworks Solutions Officer Robert Terry Announces Plan to Sell 43,374 Shares Valued at $3.58 Million - Kalkine Medi